msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The set of token names an IR defines."
msgstr "Mängden tokennamn som ett IR definierar."

#: packages/utils/src/functions/tokenUtilitiesCss.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Build token-driven utility classes: one class per token, applying it to its natural CSS property. The\ntoken's `--instui-` tail is the class name, so `--instui-font-weight-body-strong` under property\n`font-weight` yields\n`.<prefix>-font-weight-body-strong { font-weight: var(--instui-font-weight-body-strong); }`. Use it for\nevery \"one token → one property\" family (font-family/weight, line-height, border-radius, border-width,\nopacity, box-shadow). Colour and spacing keep their own builders — one token maps to several\nproperties there. Pass the token names per property (e.g. filtered from `@pantoken/tokens`)."
msgstr "Build token-driven utility classes: one class per token, applying it to its natural CSS property. The\ntoken's `--instui-` tail is the class name, so `--instui-font-weight-body-strong` under property\n`font-weight` yields\n`.&lt;prefix&gt;-font-weight-body-strong { font-weight: var(--instui-font-weight-body-strong); }`. Use it for\nevery \"one token → one property\" family (font-family/weight, line-height, border-radius, border-width,\nopacity, box-shadow). Colour and spacing keep their own builders — one token maps to several\nproperties there. Pass the token names per property (e.g. filtered from `@pantoken/tokens`)."

#: packages/utils/src/functions/tokenUtilitiesCss.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
